 "construction": "Cahn (1962) coherent spinodal and coherent miscibility gap for BCC_A2 of the two Cr-Ni set E fits.\n\nCoherent spinodal (Kunselman et al., 02_theory.tex; Cahn 1962):  d2G/dx2 + 2 eta^2 Y V_m = 0\n  Y (cubic): (C11+2C12)(C11-C12)/C11           if 2C44 - C11 + C12 > 0   (soft <100>)\n             6(C11+2C12)C44/(4C44+C11+2C12)    if 2C44 - C11 + C12 < 0   (soft <111>)\n  eta = (1/a) da/dx (Vegard), V_m = a^3 N_A / 2 (bcc).\nCoherent miscibility gap (Cahn 1962, constant eta, Y, V_m): common tangent of\n  G_coh(x; x0) = G_chem(x) + eta^2 Y V_m (x - x0)^2 .\nExpanding, the x0-dependent terms are linear in x (-2k x0 x + k x0^2), and linear terms do not change\na common-tangent construction, so the coherent tie-line ends are those of G_chem + k x^2 (k = eta^2 Y V_m),\nthe same for every overall composition x0; an alloy x0 lies in the coherent gap when it falls between them.\nBCC_A2 alone is considered (metastable bcc+bcc w.r.t. FCC/LIQUID); the stable diagram is overlaid.",
